kilograms traveling at a speed of $v$ meters per second is given by the function $K$, where $K(v)=\\frac{9}{2}v^2$. Which of the following is the best interpretation of $K(34)=5{,}202$ in this context?","A) The object traveling at 34 meters per second has a kinetic energy of 5,202 joules.","B) The object traveling at 340 meters per second has a kinetic energy of 5,202 joules.","C) The object traveling at 5,202 meters per second has a kinetic energy of 34 joules.","D) The object traveling at 23,409 meters per second has a kinetic energy of 34 joules."],"source_crop":{"x":36,"y":116,"width":242,"height":300},"needs_visual":false,"visual_crop":null,"visual_after_line":null,"question_mode":"text","content_status":"verified"},{"id":"practice-test-5:math2-11","question_lines":["The scatterplot shows the relationship between two variables $x$ and $y$. A line of best fit for the data is also shown.","For how many of the 10 data points is the actual $y$-value greater than the $y$-value predicted by the line of best fit?","A) 3","B) 4","C) 6","D) 7"],"source_crop":{"x":314,"y":116,"width":258,"height":365},"needs_visual":true,"visual_crop":{"x":0.12,"y":0.14,"width":0.76,"height":0.47},"visual_after_line":0,"question_mode":"text","content_status":"verified"},{"id":"practice-test-5:math2-12","question_lines":["At a movie theater, there are a total of 350 customers. Each customer is located in either theater A, theater B, or theater C. If one of these customers is selected at random, the probability of selecting a customer who is located in theater A is 0.48, and the probability of selecting a customer who is located in theater B is 0.24. How many customers are located in theater C?","A) 28","B) 40","C) 84","D) 98"],"source_crop":{"x":54,"y":116,"width":242,"height":270},"needs_visual":false,"visual_crop":null,"visual_after_line":null,"question_mode":"text","content_status":"verified"},{"id":"practice-test-5:math2-13","question_lines":["What is the slope of the graph of $y=\\frac{1}{3}(29x+10)+5x$ in the $xy$-plane?"],"source_crop":{"x":54,"y":385,"width":242,"height":150},"needs_visual":false,"visual_crop":null,"visual_after_line":null,"question_mode":"text","content_status":"verified"},{"id":"practice-test-5:math2-14","question_lines":["The length of each edge of a box is 29 inches. Each side of the box is in the shape of a square. The box does not have a lid. What is the exterior surface area, in square inches, of this box without a lid?"],"source_crop":{"x":54,"y":542,"width":242,"height":120},"needs_visual":false,"visual_crop":null,"visual_after_line":null,"question_mode":"text","content_status":"verified"},{"id":"practice-test-5:math2-15","question_lines":["Five Eretmochelys imbricata, a type of sea turtle, each have a nest. The table shows an original data set of the number of eggs that each turtle laid in its nest.","Nest Number of eggs","A 149","B 144","C 148","D 136","E 139","A sixth nest with 121 eggs is added to create a new data set. Which of the following correctly compares the means of the two data sets?","A) The mean of the original data set is greater than the mean of the new data set.","B) The mean of the original data set is less than the mean of the new data set.","C) The means of both data sets are equal.","D) There is not enough information to compare the means."],"source_crop":{"x":331,"y":116,"width":242,"height":385},"needs_visual":false,"visual_crop":null,"visual_after_line":null,"question_mode":"text","content_status":"verified"},{"id":"practice-test-5:math2-16","question_lines":["In $\\triangle RST$, the measure of $\\angle R$ is $63^\\circ$. Which of the following could be the measure, in degrees, of $\\angle S$?","A) 116","B) 118","C) 126","D) 180"],"source_crop":{"x":331,"y":502,"width":242,"height":130},"needs_visual":false,"visual_crop":null,"visual_after_line":null,"question_mode":"text","content_status":"verified"},{"id":"practice-test-5:math2-17","question_lines":["Which expression is equivalent to $(8x^3+8)-(x^3-2)$?","A) $8x^3+6$","B) $7x^3+10$","C) $8x^3+10$","D) $7x^3+6$"],"source_crop":{"x":36,"y":116,"width":242,"height":220},"needs_visual":false,"visual_crop":null,"visual_after_line":null,"question_mode":"text","content_status":"verified"},{"id":"practice-test-5:math2-18","question_lines":["If $4\\sqrt{2x}=16$, what is the value of $6x$?","A) 24","B) 48","C) 72","D) 96"],"source_crop":{"x":36,"y":337,"width":242,"height":160},"needs_visual":false,"visual_crop":null,"visual_after_line":null,"question_mode":"text","content_status":"verified"},{"id":"practice-test-5:math2-19","question_lines":["$$2x-y>883$$","For which of the following tables are all the values of $x$ and their corresponding values of $y$ solutions to the given inequality?","A) x: 440, 441, 442; y: 0, −2, −4","B) x: 440, 442, 441; y: 0, −2, −4","C) x: 442, 440, 441; y: 0, −2, −4","D) x: 442, 441, 440; y: 0, −2, −4"],"source_crop":{"x":314,"y":116,"width":258,"height":455},"needs_visual":false,"visual_crop":null,"visual_after_line":null,"question_mode":"text","content_status":"verified"},{"id":"practice-test-5:math2-20","question_lines":["$$\\begin{aligned}5y&=10x+11\\\\-5y&=5x-21\\end{aligned}$$","The solution to the given system of equations is $(x,y)$. What is the value of $30x$?"],"source_crop":{"x":314,"y":581,"width":258,"height":135},"needs_visual":false,"visual_crop":null,"visual_after_line":null,"question_mode":"text","content_status":"verified"},{"id":"practice-test-5:math2-21","question_lines":["A rectangle is inscribed in a circle, such that each vertex of the rectangle lies on the circumference of the circle. The diagonal of the rectangle is twice the length of the shortest side of the rectangle. The area of the rectangle is $1{,}089\\sqrt{3}$ square units. What is the length, in units, of the diameter of the circle?"],"source_crop":{"x":54,"y":116,"width":242,"height":205},"needs_visual":false,"visual_crop":null,"visual_after_line":null,"question_mode":"text","content_status":"verified"},{"id":"practice-test-5:math2-22","question_lines":["Rectangles $ABCD$ and $EFGH$ are similar. The length of each side of $EFGH$ is 6 times the length of the corresponding side of $ABCD$. The area of $ABCD$ is 54 square units. What is the area, in square units, of $EFGH$?","A) 9","B) 36","C) 324","D) 1,944"],"source_crop":{"x":54,"y":321,"width":242,"height":170},"needs_visual":false,"visual_crop":null,"visual_after_line":null,"question_mode":"text","content_status":"verified"},{"id":"practice-test-5:math2-23","question_lines":["Which expression is equivalent to $\\frac{42a}{k}+42ak$, where $k>0$?","A) $\\frac{84a}{k}$","B) $\\frac{84ak^2}{k}$","C) $\\frac{42a(k+1)}{k}$","D) $\\frac{42a(k^2+1)}{k}$"],"source_crop":{"x":331,"y":116,"width":242,"height":300},"needs_visual":false,"visual_crop":null,"visual_after_line":null,"question_mode":"text","content_status":"verified"},{"id":"practice-test-5:math2-24","question_lines":["Which quadratic equation has no real solutions?","A) $x^2+14x-49=0$","B) $x^2-14x+49=0$","C) $5x^2-14x-49=0$","D) $5x^2-14x+49=0$"],"source_crop":{"x":331,"y":422,"width":242,"height":170},"needs_visual":false,"visual_crop":null,"visual_after_line":null,"question_mode":"text","content_status":"verified"},{"id":"practice-test-5:math2-25","question_lines":["$$P(t)=260(1.04)^{\\frac{6}{4}t}$$","The function $P$ models the population, in thousands, of a certain city $t$ years after 2003. According to the model, the population is predicted to increase by 4% every $n$ months. What is the value of $n$?","A) 8","B) 12","C) 18","D) 72"],"source_crop":{"x":36,"y":116,"width":242,"height":245},"needs_visual":false,"visual_crop":null,"visual_after_line":null,"question_mode":"text","content_status":"verified"},{"id":"practice-test-5:math2-26","question_lines":["A circle in the $xy$-plane has its center at $(-1,1)$. Line $t$ is tangent to this circle at the point $(5,-4)$. Which of the following points also lies on line $t$?","A) $\\left(0,\\frac{6}{5}\\right)$","B) $(4,7)$","C) $(10,2)$","D) $(11,1)$"],"source_crop":{"x":36,"y":373,"width":242,"height":230},"needs_visual":false,"visual_crop":null,"visual_after_line":null,"question_mode":"text","content_status":"verified"},{"id":"practice-test-5:math2-27","question_lines":["For an electric field passing through a flat surface perpendicular to it, the electric flux of the electric field through the surface is the product of the electric field’s strength and the area of the surface. A certain flat surface consists of two adjacent squares, where the side length, in meters, of the larger square is 3 times the side length, in meters, of the smaller square. An electric field with strength 29.00 volts per meter passes uniformly through this surface, which is perpendicular to the electric field. If the total electric flux of the electric field through this surface is 4,640 volts · meters, what is the electric flux, in volts · meters, of the electric field through the larger square?"],"source_crop":{"x":314,"y":116,"width":258,"height":300},"needs_visual":false,"visual_crop":null,"visual_after_line":null,"question_mode":"text","content_status":"verified"}]'::jsonb) as x(
